# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need. Every name below is
# declared in src/server/env.ts, which is the only place this application
# reads process.env; tests/server-env.test.ts fails when the two drift apart.

# Credential for the OpenAI models this application calls. Optional: left
# blank, the fake adapter still answers, so `pnpm dev` works and no test
# reaches the network.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Shared secret a caller of POST /api/ask must send as `Authorization: Bearer
# <value>`. Optional while the fake adapter answers, and required as soon as
# src/server/composition.ts wires an adapter that bills a provider:
# readServerEnv refuses that combination, so a deployment that pays for
# answers cannot leave the endpoint open. Setting the key above does not on its
# own require this one -- what the endpoint costs to answer does. It buys
# authentication only: this application ships no rate limit.
API_ACCESS_KEY=
